+Cost carries a three-way `cost_status` in Mission Control's executor state:
+`reported` when the runtime itself declared a dollar figure (Claude's
+`total_cost_usd`), `derived` when no figure was reported but trusted observed
+token usage exists on a hosted (non-local) executor, and `unavailable`
+otherwise. A derived cost is a blended-rate estimate from observed tokens,
+tagged `source: 'derived-tokens'`, and never overrides or is conflated with a
+reported figure. Locally hosted models (`local_provider` set) and untrusted or
+missing observations never derive a cost.
